Package: kite-storage
Version: 1.1.2
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: KiteOS builder <root@localhost>
Recommends: libnotify-bin
Depends: bash, apt, dpkg, coreutils, diffutils, util-linux, fdisk, e2fsprogs, udev, yad, pkexec, sudo, mate-polkit, python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0
Description: KiteOS App Centre — install apps and keep them on an external disk
 App Centre (kite-app-centre) finds, installs and removes apps, updates
 KiteOS and the system, and with the kite-storage command keeps apps and
 their settings and data on an external USB/SD disk: apps are installed on
 the internal disk, then their program files and/or data are copied to the
 external disk and linked back with symlinks. Moved apps keep upgrading
 normally; APT refuses to touch them while the disk is unplugged, and their
 launchers explain what is missing.
